# The Guardian of Forever ({3} legendary artifact creature, 0/6, defender). On turn 1 it is cast with no other creature around
# it but Kobolds of Kher Keep, and with four mana floating the activation is refused all the same: "another nontoken
# creature" is not the Guardian itself and a token would not do (CR 109.1, 111.1, 118.3). On turn 3 the Kobolds, which could
# attack, is kept out of combat and the Guardian is refused as an attacker while it is neither tapped nor summoning sick
# (CR 702.3). It is then sacrificed as part of the activation's cost, paid exactly {4} from four Moxen with the pool empty
# afterwards (CR 601.2h, 608.2h), and the delayed ability returns that card - the same object - under Bot1's control at the
# beginning of that turn's end step (CR 603.7c, 400.7).

